    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW21huT9EaULKnUdD6fEmC9Nb)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Based on `main`; independent of every other open PR.\n- Touches `sp-citations.el` and its doc `sp-academic.org` (the `Citar` section only); a text conflict is possible with other PRs editing that section (e.g. #439 italic citekey): keep both sides.\n- If merged out of order: nothing breaks; `C-c b` is unchanged.\n- After merging: restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`); nothing to retarget.\n\n## Summary\n\n- **Request:** insert a citation and be asked for the page right away, under a binding different from the normal insert, so that not every citation gets a page.\n- **New command** `sp-citations-insert-with-page`, bound to `C-c B` in Org buffers.\n  - `C-c b` (`org-cite-insert`) is unchanged and never asks.\n  - Choose references with `citar-select-refs`; then one prompt per key.\n  - Result: `[cite:@key p. 12]`; several keys: `[cite:@a p. 3; @b]`.\n- **Prompt default:** the first page of the entry's BibTeX `pages` field (`12--30` gives `12`; a chapter uses its own `pages`). Delete it and press RET for no page (`@key` alone).\n- **Answer format:** `12` becomes `p. 12`, `12-14` becomes `pp. 12-14`, anything else (`ch. 3`) is kept as typed.\n- **Inside an existing citation** on the same line: the new keys are added before the closing bracket with `; `.\n- **Binding choice:** `C-c B` is the capital of the existing local `C-c b`; Org buffers only, GUI only, no `C-z/C-c/C-x/C-v` root, no `SPC`, no global key taken (checked: `C-c B` is unbound anywhere in the modules). Like `C-c b` it is a mode-local key and moves with it when the leader keymaps of the design in #278 are built.\n- Docs: bullet section in `sp-academic.org`, `.el` re-tangled (`tools/check-tangle.sh` clean).\n- Tests: `tests/sp-citations-page-test.el`, 10 ERT tests pass on Emacs 29.3 batch (first page, locator format, one/several keys, empty answer, joining an existing citation, non-Org buffer, no selection). `when-let*`/`if-let*` only. No CHANGELOG edit.\n- **Not tested with real Citar:** `citar-select-refs` and `citar-get-value` are stubbed; the real prompt and the `pages` field of your bibliography have not been run.\n\n## Manual testing\n\nMac, `~/.config/emacs-modular`, an Org buffer.\n\n- [ ] Check out: `cd ~/dotfiles; git fetch origin 445-citar-insert-with-page; git checkout 445-citar-insert-with-page`, restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`)\n- [ ] Unit tests: `cd ~/.config/emacs-modular; emacs -Q --batch -l ert -l tests/sp-citations-page-test.el -f ert-run-tests-batch-and-exit` → 10 pass\n- [ ] `C-c b` still inserts a citation without any page question\n- [ ] `C-c B`, pick an article with a `pages` field: the prompt starts with its first page; RET gives `[cite:@key p. N]`\n- [ ] `C-c B`, pick a book chapter (own `pages`): the prompt starts with the chapter's first page\n- [ ] Delete the prefilled page and press RET: `[cite:@key]`\n- [ ] Type `12-14` → `pp. 12-14`; type `ch. 3` → kept as typed\n- [ ] Select two references with TAB/M-RET: two prompts, `[cite:@a p. 3; @b]`\n- [ ] Point inside an existing `[cite:@old]`, `C-c B`: new key added with `; `\n- [ ] A key without `pages`: prompt starts empty\n- [ ] Export (`C-c C-e`) a note with `[cite:@key p. 12]` and check the locator appears in the reference\n- [ ] Regression: `C-c w b o` (`citar-open`) and citekey hover still work\n\n<details><summary>Revert after testing</summary>\n\n- Discard local edits: `git -C ~/dotfiles status`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles restore .`.\n- Back to main: `git -C ~/dotfiles switch main`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles pull`; restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`).\n- Delete any test citations you inserted in notes (`git -C ~/notes restore .` if the vault is under git).\n- Fish shell works for all of the above; no yadm steps.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiALmz9Cg7qSH4Fgzob)_",
